{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2121 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f331cdcf26e4d9fba4c7cacce2369e6cbe1ecece9298182ec4e30a52db4dce53" :edb/db-before-t 2120 :edb/db-after-t 2121 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535433 50 #inst "2026-10-09T00:00:06.345Z" 13194139535433 true] [17592186157301 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348900 13194139535433 true] [17592186157301 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348907 13194139535433 true] [17592186348900 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348901 13194139535433 true] [17592186348900 1089 "q-89876" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348900 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535433 true] [17592186348900 1100 "The function $y=f(x)$ satisfies the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y+2x.\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven that the point $P(0,-1)$ lies on the graph of the function, evaluate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at $P.$" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348900 1113 #uuid "b03dd7a9-474a-5ef8-b096-f3a65f8f342e" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348900 1145 "To find an expression for the second derivative, we differentiate the equation with respect to $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y+2x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the given expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ into the above and simplify the resulting expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =(y+2x)+2 \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =y+2x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the coordinates of our point into the above expression for the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}|}_{(0,-1)} & ={(y+2x+2)|}_{(0,-1)} \\\\  & =-1+2(0)+2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348902 13194139535433 true] [17592186348901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348903 13194139535433 true] [17592186348901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348904 13194139535433 true] [17592186348901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348905 13194139535433 true] [17592186348901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348906 13194139535433 true] [17592186348901 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535433 true] [17592186348901 1041 "selection" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348901 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348903 13194139535433 true] [17592186348901 1110 #uuid "80d5d792-c634-530d-b38f-581f783df1f7" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348902 1034 "3" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348902 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535433 true] [17592186348902 1111 #uuid "d6f09894-745c-5512-a3a4-f3906fb13303" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348903 1034 "1" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348903 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535433 true] [17592186348903 1111 #uuid "cff59460-e010-5a83-830f-5102724fe809" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348904 1034 "-4" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348904 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535433 true] [17592186348904 1111 #uuid "aadac8fe-099c-5fce-b6ea-f4485731b705" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348905 1034 "0" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348905 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535433 true] [17592186348905 1111 #uuid "f57cf218-7869-5a35-8824-d99a645722e0" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348906 1034 "-2" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348906 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535433 true] [17592186348906 1111 #uuid "4fc253ea-4ae9-5a7b-8f0e-f1d499dc9c10" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348907 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348908 13194139535433 true] [17592186348907 1089 "q-89884" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348907 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535433 true] [17592186348907 1100 "The function $y=f(x)$ satisfies the differential equation ${y}^{′}={e}^{y}+x.$ Given that the point $(-1,0)$ lies on the graph of the function, what is the value of ${{y}^{″}|}_{(-1,0)}?$" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348907 1113 #uuid "54ef928c-296a-5b56-8027-31cba563faf2" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348907 1145 "To find an expression for the second derivative, we differentiate the equation with respect to $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}^{′})^{′} & ={({e}^{y}+x)}^{′} \\\\ ({y}^{′})^{′} & ={({e}^{y})}^{′}+{(x)}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{″} & ={y}^{′}{e}^{y}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the chain rule to compute ${({e}^{y})}^{′}.$\n\nNow, we substitute the given expression for ${y}^{′}$ into the above and simplify the resulting expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″} & ={y}^{′}{e}^{y}+1 \\\\ {y}^{″} & =({e}^{y}+x)\\cdot {e}^{y}+1 \\\\ {y}^{″} & ={e}^{2y}+x{e}^{y}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the coordinates of our point into the above expression for the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{y}^{″}|}_{(-1,0)} & ={({e}^{2y}+x{e}^{y}+1)|}_{(-1,0)} \\\\  & ={e}^{2(0)}+(-1){e}^{0}+1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348909 13194139535433 true] [17592186348908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348910 13194139535433 true] [17592186348908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348911 13194139535433 true] [17592186348908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348912 13194139535433 true] [17592186348908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348913 13194139535433 true] [17592186348908 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535433 true] [17592186348908 1041 "selection" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348908 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348912 13194139535433 true] [17592186348908 1110 #uuid "5efdb9ac-2fb5-58a5-a2b7-e4117779bf78" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348909 1034 "2e" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535433 true] [17592186348909 1111 #uuid "c127ac23-d520-5355-98ec-cb418f441597" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348910 1034 "2" 13194139535433 true] [17592186348910 1103 #edb/ref 17592